{"id":"graph-view","parent":"sd-nav","ord":"a0","title":"Graph view: the reference graph as a navigable map","todo":true,"desc":"- `/graph/<id>` shows a node's neighbourhood; `/graph` the whole reference graph. Click to navigate; files drawn as groupings.\n- PR #247 built it but is parked as a draft: the human found it unsatisfying because .md documents aren't in the graph, and bolting that on would be messy.\n- Waits on the nodes/documents unification design (brainstorming/first-class-documents.md); rebuild on addresses once that lands.","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:49-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:04:20-04:00","custom":{"blocker-restated":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: \"rebuild on addresses once that lands\" — addresses LANDED at #256 (PR 1 of first-class-documents.md's path); the live blocker is PR 2 (the one Document collection — set.ts:74 still carries a separate documents array). Note also the graph's absent file set is now SIX kinds wide (#362 gave csv/pdf/pictures addresses and pages, no vertices)","pr":"#247 parked as draft 2026-08-19 — the human ruled it unsatisfying: no .md/.olai parity, and bolting parity on would make a ball of mud; waits on the nodes/docs unification architecture (brainstorming doc)","unblocked-by":"brainstorming/first-class-documents.md — rebuilt on addresses at step 4 of its path"}}
{"id":"search-document-bodies","parent":"sd-search","ord":"a0","title":"Search inside HTML documents — needs a ruling first #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"- Search already covers markdown document bodies (shipped with #258).\n- What's left: `.html` files. Their text isn't searchable because the server deliberately doesn't keep HTML bodies in memory (they can be megabytes).\n- Needs a decision before any code: either declare HTML opaque to search and close this, or design an index that reads bodies at search time without loading them all.\n- Related: the parked semantic-recall work.","created":"2026-08-16T14:35:47-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:04:23-04:00","custom":{"scope-widened":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: the remainder is no longer just .html — #362 added csv (holds:text, kept:false — the identical not-in-memory argument) and picture/pdf (holds:bytes — a different question: extraction, not memory); all share filter.ts's Unkept Bodied arm, whose own docstring (\"a .md and a .html alike\") is now stale. The ruling this node wants splits in two: text-but-unkept (.html, .csv) vs bytes (.pdf, pictures). Cross-link: first-class-documents.md PR 2 claims to close this node"}}
{"id":"hindsight-comparison","parent":"sd-mcp","ord":"a0","title":"Olai vs Hindsight: which agent-memory features are worth adopting #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"- Comparison against hindsight.vectorize.io, keeping files as the single source of truth. Brainstorm: docs/brainstorming/hindsight.md.\n- Six recommendations: semantic search as a derived gitignored index; time/graph recall as query clauses; capture-as-proposal at conversation end; consolidation as a stale/duplicates reading; per-connection scoping for multiple agents; sync stays git.\n- Deliberately not copied: LLM-normalized notes, identity config, hosted memory.\n- Awaits the human's picks.","changed":"2026-08-24T16:04:25-04:00","custom":{"rec5-answered":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: recommendation 5 (per-connection agent scoping) is settled AGAINST by master — listings.ts:4 rules one live agent always; the scoping arrived as listing-is-a-question fan-out (#343) + the per-conversation roster (#357). Recommendation 3's capture shape predates #354 (POST /capture retired for `olai surface capture`). The live remainder is picks 1, 2, 4 re-read against those"}}
